===== 711efe05c6433151eca5c26c67ef92b7f2a20682 perf: constrain Zabbix item-id inputs and single-flight the cache miss (#1019)
perf: constrain Zabbix item-id inputs and single-flight the cache miss (#1019)

Traffic and multi-latest cache keys are minted from unvalidated client
input, letting any distinct string force fresh upstream Zabbix calls.
Validate both controllers' item ids as numeric strings (max 32 / 64)
BEFORE any cache, lock or upstream access.

Serve the cache miss through Cache::flexible([240, 300]): a request
arriving during an in-flight refresh is answered with the stale value
(no busy 503, no error-level contention logs), the refresh lock is
released even when the upstream fails, and a failed result is never
cached (the compute throws into the unchanged 503 body contract).

Test updates: numeric fixtures in multi-latest tests, non-numeric
rejection cases for both controllers, two-phase upstream recovery, and
an explicit frozen key-format assertion; tearDown now runs
parent::tearDown() before Mockery::close() so an unmet expectation can
no longer strand the RefreshDatabase transaction.

phpstan-baseline regenerated: 6 entries removed, 0 added.
===== efebf793657626594fabf181a445704313bcc682 perf: switch the Excel exports to FromQuery so chunking actually engages
perf: switch the Excel exports to FromQuery so chunking actually engages

HardwareExport and HardwareAuditsExport declared WithChunkReading, but that
interface only exists on the import path (Reader.php:89); the export path
consults WithCustomChunkSize (Sheet.php:854) — so three exports materialised
the whole filtered set via collection() before a single row was written, and
HardwareAuditsExport::chunkCollection() was dead code with zero call sites.

- HardwareExport/HardwareAuditsExport: FromCollection + WithChunkReading
  replaced with FromQuery + WithCustomChunkSize; collection() and the dead
  chunkCollection()/ machinery deleted; query() hands over the
  controller's builder untouched (alias columns, scope, filters included).
- HardwareAuditsExport::query() keeps latest('created_at') and adds
  orderBy('id') as tie-breaker: library chunking is LIMIT/OFFSET and
  created_at has second precision, so same-second rows could silently
  repeat or drop between chunks (pinned red by test without the tie-breaker).
- PersonsExport: constructor now takes the builder directly (decided 1-الف);
  the controller no longer ->get()s the whole filtered set. Eager loads
  stay on the controller's builder so no chunk pays an N+1.
  config/excel.php, UnitsExport and app/Imports are untouched; this change
